 ## Background
-The standard Marching Cubes algorithm by Lorensen and Cline (1987) uses a 12-case lookup table, ignoring the topological ambiguities present in the remaining 256-12=244 cases [774-marching-cubes.md] [G]. This led to topological errors, such as the "tunnel" problem where a single tunnel is rendered as two separate sheets [G]. Early work by Williams (1990) and others identified these ambiguities [G]. The Asymptotic Decider was introduced to resolve 2D ambiguities using bilinear interpolation [790-asymptotic-decider.md]. In 3D, various approaches emerged: [1368-topologically-correct-marching-cubes.md] proposed inserting vertices to match the trilinear interpolant; [1618-extended-trilinear-triangulation.md] (MC33) used a 33-case table based on trilinear analysis; and [1428-topologically-defined-isosurfaces.md] / [1430-topologically-defined-isosurface-via-connectedness-couples.md] focused on binary volumes using digital topology and connectedness couples. [961-marching-cubes-with-hermite-data-and-full-case-table.md] explored higher-order interpolation for geometric accuracy.
+The standard Marching Cubes algorithm by Lorensen and Cline (1987) uses a 12-case lookup table, ignoring the topological ambiguities present in the remaining 256-12=244 cases [774-marching-cubes.md] [G]. This led to topological errors, such as the "tunnel" problem where a single tunnel is rendered as two separate sheets [G]. Early work by Williams (1990) and others identified these ambiguities [G]. The Asymptotic Decider was introduced to resolve 2D ambiguities using bilinear interpolation [Asymptotic Decider](790-asymptotic-decider.md). In 3D, various approaches emerged: [Topologically Correct Marching Cubes](1368-topologically-correct-marching-cubes.md) proposed inserting vertices to match the trilinear interpolant; [Extended Trilinear Triangulation](1618-extended-trilinear-triangulation.md) (MC33) used a 33-case table based on trilinear analysis; and [Topologically Defined Isosurfaces](1428-topologically-defined-isosurfaces.md) / [Topologically Defined Isosurface via Connectedness Couples](1430-topologically-defined-isosurface-via-connectedness-couples.md) focused on binary volumes using digital topology and connectedness couples. [Marching Cubes with Hermite Data and Full Case Table](961-marching-cubes-with-hermite-data-and-full-case-table.md) explored higher-order interpolation for geometric accuracy.
 
